<title>JAPAN: Canada, China to agree on pork standard - chief.</title>
<headline>Canada, China to agree on pork standard - chief.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canada and China are likely to reach an agreement on quality standards for pork exports within a year, and promote direct shipments of the meat to China, the head of the Canadian pork industry trade group said.</p>
<p>&quot;The two governments are discussing pork quality standards and may agree within one year,&quot; Jim Morris, president of Canada Pork International, told Reuters in an interview.</p>
<p>&quot;Some pork exports to Hong Kong goes to China unofficially. When China officially recognizes our pork quality standard, we'll be allowed to export to China,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>Canada exported 341,058 tonnes of pork in 1995. Of that, 16,375 tonnes went to Hong Kong.</p>
<p>Morris is currently visiting Tokyo with meat industry officials to promote exports to Japanese market. -- Tokyo Commodity Desk (81-3-3432-7391)</p>
